scope: |
  SPRINT Batch E3 = specs/portable-save-region.md §6 slice 4 — EFFECTFUL REGION (Fx closed):
  a region whose body performs effects HANDLED INSIDE the region.
  FIRST STEP IS A MEASUREMENT, not the CPS the spec hypothesises. Effect prims are ordinary
  CoreIR Prims (Runtime.scala:1231 -> PortableEffects.eval): effect.perform(label, args...),
  effect.handle(computation, handler), effect.pure(v); a plain Lam(1,..) handler always
  HandlerDispatch.Matched (Runtime.dispatchHandler1:202). SaveRegion's freeOuterIndices/rewrite/
  globalsOf already treat Prim generically. So a CLOSED effectful region may ALREADY reify and run
  machine-less — measure before writing a CPS pass.
  The second half is the boundary: an effect that ESCAPES the region (handler outside) must fail
  CLOSED, not silently return an Op value. Check that too — same fail-open shape as the frame hole
  just closed in E2 (BUGS portable-capsule-frame-unvalidated).
